&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192411/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1793798261/pdysphxg4hnrkojir9jv.png" width="640" style="    line-height: 100%;      "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192411/rss" title="mofu-dev.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Spreading Liquid with Three.js&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A technical walkthrough of a neat liquid-spreading effect (built for a cosmetics campaign). It shows off using a height map for thickness, a velocity map for movement, and fragment shaders to render the result. There's a satisfying demo to play with, too.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;MISAKI NAKANO &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192412/rss" title="www.ivankristianto.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;How a Split Webfont Slowed Down Text Layout&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A font splitter put &lt;code&gt;i&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;j&lt;/code&gt; in a different file from the rest of the alphabet, forcing extra text-shaping work within words (causing INP to suffer). Here's why, plus a script to check your own font CSS.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Ivan Kristianto &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192413/rss" title="www.tigerdata.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Why Is the Analytics Tab the Slowest Page in Your App?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Usually it's one query scanning months of rows. TimescaleDB extends Postgres to make it fast. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192413/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Get $1000 credit&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Tiger Data (creators of TimescaleDB) &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192414/rss" title="blog.master.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Multi-Column Different-Speed Scrolling&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — There are some fun scrolling experiments here thanks to scroll-driven animations.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Chris Coyier &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192415/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;"&gt;Useful &lt;code&gt;@custom-media&lt;/code&gt; Presets&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;"&gt;Daniel Schwarz&lt;/span&gt; 
  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;"&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;⚠️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;Third-Party Scripts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Last week we &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192416/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;shared a PSA about forgotten script tags&lt;/a&gt; and how what they load can be hijacked. Days later, a similar attack prominently appeared in the wild.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On October 29, &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192417/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;a performance monitoring script on Polymarket was swapped for a wallet drainer&lt;/a&gt;. The URL of the script didn't change, just the payload, so the CSP let it through, but Scott Helme's write-up explains what would have stopped it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whatever you load from third parties, it's worth auditing for security, privacy, &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; performance reasons. Some steps worth taking:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pin scripts with &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192418/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Subresource Integrity&lt;/a&gt; where the vendor's file is static, and use the new &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192419/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Integrity-Policy-Report-Only&lt;/code&gt; header&lt;/a&gt; to find any you've missed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192420/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Self-host third-party resources&lt;/a&gt; where you can. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192421/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Request Metrics explains&lt;/a&gt; how it protects its own agent and why it's safe to self-host.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192422/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Load third-party JavaScript efficiently&lt;/a&gt;, or use &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192423/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Partytown&lt;/a&gt; to move it off the main thread entirely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit what your page is loading with &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192424/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Request Map&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192425/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Third Party Web&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lastly, if &lt;em&gt;you&lt;/em&gt; provide third-party scripts to users, check out Jack Ellis's &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192443/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;writeup of how Fathom Analytics keeps their analytics script secure&lt;/a&gt; for some tips.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
