     &lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192087/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1793190176/dlisimtjkn0bavqwusxs.png" width="640" style="      line-height: 100%;  "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;🖼️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192087/rss" title="developer.chrome.com" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;"&gt;HTML-in-Canvas: Interactive DOM Inside 2D, WebGL and WebGPU Canvases&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Arriving in stable Chrome next week, this long-incubated API draws real, live HTML into 2D, WebGL and WebGPU canvases, with text selection, form controls, Find-in-Page and screen readers all still working. Three.js, Babylon.js and PixiJS already support it. Chrome-only for now, but a big leap for canvas-heavy UIs. There's &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192088/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;a related video here too&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Natalia Markoborodova (Chrome) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192089/rss" title="blog.master.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Creating Dynamic Social Media Cards for User Content&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Chris digs into how links unfurl across Discord, X, Slack, Bluesky, iMessage and more, and argues most dynamic social cards waste the image by just restating the title and description. Then he shows what &lt;em&gt;should&lt;/em&gt; go on it instead.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Chris Coyier &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192126/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/2883b63b.png" width="110" height="110" style="padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px;     line-height: 100%; "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192126/rss" title="www.meticulous.ai" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Would You Let Your AI Agent Grade Its Own Homework?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Agents write code faster than ever. They even review their own work. But who’s reviewing them? Dropbox, Notion &amp;amp; ElevenLabs don’t take the risk. With Meticulous, every change is exhaustively verified, with zero developer effort.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Meticulous &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192090/rss" title="blog.report-uri.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;DeadTag: Forgotten Third-Party Script Tags Became a Delivery Network for Spyware&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Attackers are buying up expired domains once used by analytics, ad and widget scripts, so any site still carrying the old tag now silently loads attacker code. A worthy reminder to go audit those tags!&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Scott Helme &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;"&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;⚡️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;IN BRIEF&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192091/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;CSS-Tricks&lt;/a&gt;, after a spell under the ownership of DigitalOcean, is &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192092/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;independent once again&lt;/a&gt; under the stewardship of editor &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192093/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Geoff Graham&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🦊 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192094/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Firefox 159&lt;/a&gt; enables scroll-driven animations by default, so they now work in all major engines. It also adds scoped custom element registries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🪪 Since Chrome 155, sites can &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192095/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;use the Digital Credentials API to offer credentials&lt;/a&gt;, such as digital IDs, to a compatible wallet app on the user's phone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚙️ W3C has launched &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192096/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;a polyfill pilot for WebMCP&lt;/a&gt;, a JavaScript API that exposes web app functionality as agent-callable tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌅 The &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192097/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Arc browser is being sunset&lt;/a&gt; this December, and &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192098/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Dia is suggested&lt;/a&gt; as a viable alternative. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192099/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Zen&lt;/a&gt; is another, non-Chromium variant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📺 Firefox has &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192100/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;▶️ a new ad with various 'meme icons'&lt;/a&gt; from years gone by (Numa Numa Guy kicks things off).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;📙&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;"&gt;Articles, Opinions &amp;amp; Tutorials&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192101/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1793184512/znxptwkdwyktd3mp9ul6.png" width="640" style="    line-height: 100%;      "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192101/rss" title="webkit.org" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;WebKit Features for Safari 27.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A fresh release of Safari came out alongside Apple's new foldable. There's advice on how to create layouts for folding screens using &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192102/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Device Posture API&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192103/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Viewport Segments API&lt;/a&gt;. Both are behind feature flags for now.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Jen Simmons (WebKit) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;&lt;p&gt;💡 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192104/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Safari 27.2 followed days later&lt;/a&gt;, adding &lt;code&gt;::field-content&lt;/code&gt; for styling a customizable select's displayed text, and renaming Grid Lanes' &lt;code&gt;flow-tolerance&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;fit-tolerance&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192105/rss" title="paulcalvano.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Investigating a Curious Case of Font Format Fallbacks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Paul chases a bug in which a site's font loaded &lt;em&gt;three times in a row&lt;/em&gt;, as WOFF2, then WOFF, then TTF, following the browser's error messages into Chromium's own source to find the cause.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Paul Calvano &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;🗓️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192106/rss" title="sentry.io" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Workshop: How to Implement Session Replay&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Filters, custom tags, and sampling settings for finding the sessions that matter. Nov 5, 10am PT.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Sentry &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192107/rss" title="csswizardry.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Performance Budgets Need a Representative Worst&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Harry revises his own long-standing advice: a budget set from your single worst result lets one outlier hide real regressions, so start from a &lt;em&gt;representative worst&lt;/em&gt; (P90 or P95 of recent data) instead. A spreadsheet template is included.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Harry Roberts &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;▶  &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192108/rss" title="www.youtube.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Most Vulnerable Week in Internet History&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A fast recap of a rough security week: PHP2Shell (a pair of PHP engine bugs allowing unauthenticated RCE), a backdoored LiteLLM release, a CA with private keys that were numbers under 256, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Fireship &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192109/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1793183383/ema2hdklrxos6pdignjh.png" width="640" style="    line-height: 100%;      "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192109/rss" title="blog.master.dev" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Building an Isolated Preview for AI-Generated HTML&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Any app that lets a model generate UI has to render the HTML it hands back. Keshav builds five demos showing how a preview can be attacked, then hardens it with iframe sandboxing, CSP and a carefully checked &lt;code&gt;postMessage&lt;/code&gt; handler.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Keshav Malik &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;🖨️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192110/rss" title="brennenputh.me" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Websites Should Be Printable&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Brennen printed his own site, didn't like the result, and walks through the print stylesheet changes that fixed it: a hidden header, 12pt type, and black links.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Brennen Puth &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.0em; color: #000;"&gt;▶  &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192111/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1em !important; font-weight: 500 !important;"&gt;Why I'm Still Making CSS Tutorials&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — On caring about the craft of little details and why they matter in an age of agentic code generation.
  &lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color: #5a5a5a; margin-top: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6em !important;"&gt;Kevin Powell&lt;/span&gt; 
  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;🧰&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.4em;"&gt;Tools, Code &amp;amp; Resources&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192112/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/w_1280,e_sharpen:60,q_auto/v1793184989/nryxba3xm0aht3jljc6s.png" width="640" style="    line-height: 100%;      "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192112/rss" title="titleart.dvy.io" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;TitleArt: Make Text Like It's 1997&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Aww yeah, a big dose of nostalgia for users of Microsoft Office back in the 90s. Every classic WordArt style, shape and 3-D effect recreated in the browser.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Davey Barker &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192113/rss" title="www.tigerdata.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The “Last 90 Days” Filter Shouldn’t Need a Spinner&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Bigger date ranges mean your chart’s query scans more rows. TimescaleDB keeps it fast in Postgres. &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192113/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Get $1000 credit&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Tiger Data (creators of TimescaleDB) &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192114/rss" title="specification.website" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The Website Specification: Every Technical Detail a Site Needs Before Launch&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A checklist you (or an agent) can work through before launch, covering SEO, accessibility, security, performance, privacy, i18n, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Joost de Valk &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/192115/rss" title="whisper.tanpreet.xyz" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;browser-whisper 2.0: In-Browser Audio and Video Transcription with WebGPU&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A library that runs Whisper, Moonshine and other speech models entirely in the browser over WebGPU (with a WASM fallback), complete with timestamped segments, cached models and live mic input.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Tanpreet Singh Jolly &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

