&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;
  &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191778/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/cpress/image/upload/c_limit,w_480,h_480,q_auto/copm/e8bf0b4e.png" width="140" height="140" style="padding-top: 12px; padding-left: 12px;     line-height: 100%; "&gt;&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191778/rss" title="www.meticulous.ai" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;"&gt;Would You Let Your AI Agent Grade Its Own Homework?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Agents write code faster than ever. They even review their own work. But who’s reviewing them? Dropbox, Notion &amp;amp; ElevenLabs don’t take the risk. With Meticulous, every change is exhaustively verified, with zero developer effort.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Meticulous &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: 4px; font-size: 0.9em;   color: #997 !important; padding: 1px 4px; "&gt;sponsor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;🗳️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191790/rss" title="survey.devographics.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;The State of HTML 2026&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — The annual survey returns to measure the awareness and adoption of HTML features and browser APIs. This year covers Web Components, progressive enhancement, AI, and more. It takes less than 15 minutes and you can learn new things just by taking it.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Devographics &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 18px;"&gt;

  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191791/rss" title="webkit.org" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;Safari Blocks 'Identity Resolution' Tracking Infrastructure&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Cross-site cookies are long gone in Safari, so trackers moved to 'identity resolution' where third parties get the email address you type into forms and turn it into a cross-site, cross-device tracking ID. Safari now blocks them at the domain level.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Wilander, Wolfe, and Finkel (WebKit) &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px;"&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style=" font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em;"&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;table border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0 border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.48em; padding: 0px 15px;"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;⚡️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;IN BRIEF&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚠️ If PHP runs anywhere behind your sites: &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191792/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;PHP 8.5.12, 8.4.27, 8.3.36 and 8.2.35 fix two critical bugs&lt;/a&gt; that allow unauthenticated remote code execution. Update now, &lt;em&gt;mod_php&lt;/em&gt; installs especially.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌐 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191793/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Chrome 157 is in beta&lt;/a&gt; with &lt;code&gt;corner&lt;/code&gt; shorthands, a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;string&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; value for &lt;code&gt;text-overflow&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;anchor-valid&lt;/code&gt;. Chrome 156 went stable this week with CSS &lt;code&gt;random()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚫 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191794/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Chrome has finished deprecating the &lt;code&gt;unload&lt;/code&gt; event&lt;/a&gt;: handlers no longer fire by default, so use &lt;code&gt;pagehide&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;visibilitychange&lt;/code&gt; instead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

