  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191795/rss" title="jakearchibald.com" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;JPEG XL vs AVIF for Web Use-Cases&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — Now that JPEG XL has landed in all major browsers, Jake took the format for a spin, benchmarking it against AVIF. There's a lot of detail here with some good takeaways. You might also be surprised at &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/191796/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;what you can cram in under 200 bytes&lt;/a&gt; with JPEG XL.&lt;/p&gt;
